[?2004lSURICATA CORRELATION SCRIPT - BUG FIX SUMMARY
==============================================

PROBLEM:
The correlation script was finding 80% fewer lateral movement candidates
compared to the old Zeek-based pipeline.

ROOT CAUSE:
Two bugs in /home/user/correlate.py:

1. CRITICAL BUG - Wrong event_type:
   - Script checked for event_type == "netflow"
   - Suricata actually uses event_type == "flow"
   - Result: Script processed ZERO flow events

2. SECONDARY BUG - Wrong timestamp format:
   - Script used: "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S"
   - Suricata uses: "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S.%f%z" (with microseconds and timezone)
   - Result: Would have caused parsing errors once bug #1 was fixed

FIXES APPLIED:
- Changed event_type check from "netflow" to "flow"
- Updated timestamp parsing to handle microseconds and timezone
- Backup saved to /home/user/correlate.py.backup

RESULTS:
- Script now successfully processes internal-to-internal flow events
- Detected lateral movement candidate: 10.1.5.23
- Host 10.1.5.23 connected to 12+ distinct internal hosts within 5 minutes
- Detection pattern matches expected scanning behavior

VERIFICATION:
- Confirmed eve.json contains "flow" events (not "netflow")
- Confirmed internal-to-internal traffic exists in logs
- Confirmed timestamp format: 2024-01-10T00:00:13.316061+0000
- Script now correctly identifies scanning activity
